<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil marked lower, buying fades.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil marked lower, buying fades.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7987)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     33.30/33.70     18.51/18.73   34.00/34.40</p>
<p> BREMEN		33.30/33.70     18.51/18.73   34.00/34.40</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    32.70/34.10     18.18/18.96   34.30/34.70</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   34.40/34.80     19.12/19.35   35.00/35.40</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   34.40/34.80     19.12/19.35   35.10/35.50</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  36.00/36.40     20.01/20.24   36.80/37.20</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were marked lower on Tuesday following Mondays falls on international futures markets and Rotterdam barge prices. Traders said buying today was thin with most buyers having covered following Mondays initial price jump.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7456</p>
